{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"satiny-jeanlike-mole","creation_channel":"cli","description":"The gate that pauses reconciliation is a remote-persisted git ref `refs/reconciler/gate`\n(`_ref_lock.py:111`) whose blob holds `{\"gated_mode\": \"<mode>\"}`. `check_phase_gate`\n(`_advisory_lock.py:250`) blocks when `target_mode > gated_mode` by RANK over the five-value ladder.\nRetiring `--mode` removes that ladder, so the blob must change.\n\n**This is the highest-risk item in the epic.** `_decode_gate` (`_ref_lock.py:658`) REQUIRES a\nnon-empty `gated_mode` string and gate reads are fail-closed, so a new-format blob read by an older\nbinary does not degrade — it WEDGES every pass, fleet-wide, because the ref is shared on `origin`.\n\nDesign spike findings that must be honoured:\n\n- **The compatibility value is `gated_mode: \"reconcile-check\"`, NOT `\"dry-run\"`.** A `dry-run` gate\n  still lets a dry-run pass run to completion and exit 0, so an old binary reports GREEN while the\n  bridge is supposed to be stopped. `reconcile-check` is the bottom rung, so everything reaching the\n  check is blocked.\n- **Never use a non-Mode shim value.** `gated_mode: \"paused\"` is not a `Mode`, so `_mode_blocks`\n  catches the `ValueError` and returns `False` — a SILENT fail-open un-pause, worse than the wedge\n  because nothing is red.\n- **Reader ships first, writer never emits new-only.** Favourable condition: there is NO production\n  writer today (`set_gate`/`clear_gate` have zero callers), so no new-format blob can exist until we\n  build one. That removes all time pressure.\n- **Live bug to fix on the way:** `check_phase_gate` is called at `__main__.py:613`, OUTSIDE the\n  `try:` beginning at `:646`, so `RefLockCorruptError` escapes `main()` — raw traceback and exit 1\n  instead of a clean exit 4.\n- OSS validation confirmed `pause`/`resume` with a required reason, and `status` exiting 0 while\n  paused. One adjustment adopted: offer an optional `--until <duration>` (Argo Rollouts ships both\n  shapes). Every tool whose pause suppresses an ALERTING signal bounds it — Alertmanager makes the\n  comment mandatory and rejects zero-duration silences.\n\nCASCADE: consider caller + dynamic-reference impact when renaming `check_phase_gate`.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] The gate blob carries paused/reason/who/paused_at AND retains `gated_mode: \"reconcile-check\"`\n- [ ] `pause \"<reason>\"` and `resume` are the only supported write path; no operator uses git plumbing\n- [ ] A test vendors the PRE-CHANGE decoder verbatim and feeds it every blob the new writer can produce\n- [ ] A test asserts the compatibility value is a real Mode member, guarding the silent fail-open\n- [ ] A corrupt gate blob produces a clean exit 4 with the recovery command, not a traceback\n- [ ] `pause` detects the no-remote case and refuses loudly rather than reporting a local-only success\n- [ ] The workflow treats a paused bridge as a notice, not an error","id":"1104-93eb-6ce0-4a19","parent_id":"2f79-2b32-28c5-4eb3","priority":1,"tags":["bridge"],"ticket_type":"story","title":"Gate format migration and the pause/resume surface"},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1786047432858039001,"uuid":"c0eff637-fcd5-455f-a56b-753477de0a9f"}